      <p class="text-sm text-accent-400 mb-4">August 4, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Tattoo Safety &amp; Compliance Guide: Health Rules, Ink Rules &amp; Studio Licensing</h1>
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-ink-800">
        <img src="/images/blog/tattoo-safety-compliance-guide.svg" alt="Tattoo safety and compliance — health, ink, and licensing rules" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] object-cover" loading="eager" />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-gray-300">
        A tattoo is a deliberate, controlled wound. Whether it heals clean comes down to a stack of rules — who is allowed to operate, how they stop infection, what goes into your skin, and how you look after it. This guide covers the rules that actually exist, and every claim links to the primary regulation so you can verify it yourself.
      </p>
    </div>
